    "section_evoo_v3_faq_rRJhLR": {
      "type": "section-evoo-v3-faq",
      "blocks": {
        "faq_item_BFc6Am": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "I already take NAC. Why would I switch to NAC+?",
            "answer": "<p>AIWO NAC (600mg) is a single-ingredient product optimised for maximum NAC dose ideal for those with a specific glutathione, liver, or respiratory focus where full-dose NAC is the priority. AIWO NAC+ adds Taurine 500mg to the formula. Taurine works on entirely different pathways: cardiovascular function, GABA receptor modulation, bile acid conjugation, and cellular osmolysis.</p><p>If your health concerns span liver, heart, and nervous system NAC+ covers both in one tablet.If your sole focus is maximum glutathione, AIWO NAC 600mg remains the right product. Your physician will confirm which is right for your protocol.<br/><br/></p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_pgG9dR": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What does Taurine do that NAC does not?",
            "answer": "<p>NAC's primary action is upstream: it delivers cysteine for intracellular glutathione synthesis. Taurine is a separate sulfur-containing amino acid found in high concentrations in the heart, brain, eyes, and skeletal muscle. Its key roles include: conjugating bile acids in the liver to aid fat digestion, stabilising cardiac cell membranes and supporting heart rhythm regularity, modulating GABA activity in the brain for neurological calm, and protecting cells from osmotic and oxidative stress. These are distinct from the glutathione axis they are additive, not redundant.<br/><br/><br/></p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_zet6LP": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Who benefits most from AIWO NAC+?",
            "answer": "<p>Adults with combined concerns spanning liver health, cardiovascular function, and nervous system support. Particularly relevant for: high-stress urban professionals with elevated cortisol burden, individuals with elevated liver enzymes and cardiovascular risk markers, those in high-pollution environments with respiratory and oxidative load, and active individuals seeking both glutathione and taurine support without stacking two separate products. consult your physician before use if pregnant, nursing, or on ongoing medication.<br/><br/></p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_WyBt4K": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How long before I notice a difference?",
            "answer": "<p>Glutathione replenishment and antioxidant support build with consistent use over 30-90 days. Some individuals with high oxidative burden notice subjective improvements in energy and clarity within 2-4 weeks. Objective improvements in liver enzymes or oxidative stress biomarkers are typically measurable at the 60-90 day mark with appropriate testing. Individual results vary. If pregnant, nursing, or on medication, consult your doctor before use.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "faq_item_BFc6Am",
        "faq_item_pgG9dR",
        "faq_item_zet6LP",
        "faq_item_WyBt4K"
      ],
      "name": "EVOO v3 - FAQ",
      "settings": {
